				<r3d:description language="eng">Phytozome is the Plant Comparative Genomics portal of the Department of Energy&#039;s Joint Genome Institute. Families of related genes representing the modern descendants of ancestral genes are constructed at key phylogenetic nodes. These families allow easy access to clade-specific orthology/paralogy relationships as well as insights into clade-specific novelties and expansions.</r3d:description>
				<r3d:repositoryContact>
			<r3d:repositoryContactInformation>phytozome@jgi-psf.org</r3d:repositoryContactInformation>
			<r3d:repositoryContactType>administrative</r3d:repositoryContactType>
		</r3d:repositoryContact>
						<r3d:type>disciplinary</r3d:type>
						<r3d:size>411 assembled and annotated genomes, from 174 Archaeplastida species; 54 Brachypodium distachyon lines from the BrachyPan pan-genome study; 20 species included in the Brassicales Map Alignment Project;  8 cowpea (Vigna unguiculata) genomes included in the CowpeaPan pan-genome project</r3d:size>
